  "caption": "Quinn asked for maximum pressure. Five minutes in: \"Okay, maybe medium!\" Afterwards Quinn felt loose and wondered if the knots had been broken up.\n\nRemedial massage can ease pain and muscle tension in the short term, help you relax and sleep, and make moving feel easier. It doesn't realign the pelvis, break down knots or build tissue strength.\n\nWhat often helps: pair it with exercise, speak up about pressure (harder isn't always better), and time sessions after a big training block or a stressful week. If you need it weekly just to cope, the cause may need a closer look.\n\nCheck with a doctor first if you have unexplained pain, fever, a recent significant injury or blood clot risk.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
